READ ME

Generalised Linear Mixed Models.R is the code file used for the analyses in R.

For all files a 1 at the end represents the analyses / files used on the smaller sample size where the eggs that matched the colour of the adults were excluded.

FishEggs.csv: 
Column 1 = Species name. 
Column 2-4 = Genus, Family and Order. 
Column 5 = Pigment State. 
Column 6 = Whether the egg colour matches the adult colour. 
Column 7 = Development Score (0 = Demersal, 1 = Pelagic). 
Column 8 = Value for average depth in metres. 
Column 9 = Value for average surface temperature in degrees Celcius. 
Column 10 = Value for average oxygen concentration in μmol/m3. 
Column 11 = Value for average chlorophyll concentration in μmol/m3. 
Column 12 = Latitude in degrees. 
Column 13 = PostCare Parental Care score (0 = No Care, 1 = External Parental Care, 2 = Internal Parental Care). 
Columns 14 & 15 = PC1 and PC2 values generated from PCA for oxygen and temperature. 
NA represents missing data. 
